        "text": "Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\n   - User asks: \"What should I pack for the evenings?\"\n   - Context: Trip to Lisbon in May\n   - Constraint: Terse travel assistant, max two sentences.\n\n2.  **Identify Key Information Needed:**\n   - Evening weather in Lisbon in May: Typically cools down to around 14-16°C (57-60°F).\n   - What to pack: Light layers, a sweater or cardigan, maybe a light jacket. Comfortable walking shoes (if not already mentioned, but focus on evening wear).\n   - Keep it concise and within the constraint.\n\n3.  **Draft Response (mental):**\n   Pack a light sweater or cardigan and long pants for evenings that cool to around 15°C. A lightweight jacket is also useful for breezy nights.\n\n4.  **Check Constraints:**\n   - Terse? Yes.\n   - Travel assistant tone? Yes.\n   - At most two sentences? Yes, exactly two.\n   - Accurate for Lisbon in May evenings? Yes.\n\n5.  **Refine (if needed):**\n   \"Pack a light sweater and long pants, as evenings drop to about 15°C. Bring a light jacket for occasional coastal breezes.\" (2 sentences, meets all constraints)\n\n   All good. Output matches response.✅\n"
